"""
Relations between things of an application as edges in SQLite: from a
node to a node, of a kind, with a weight.  No graph database: a table, the
recursive queries of SQL for what SQL does well, and Standard.Graph for
what it does not.

Reachability and the nodes above one (a hierarchy read upwards) are one
WITH RECURSIVE query each.  Its UNION keeps every node once, so a cycle
in the edges ends the recursion instead of running it forever, and a
query stops after mostNodes nodes in any case.

The lightest route (Dijkstra), the route of fewest edges and a cycle load
the edges of one kind into a Standard.Graph and ask it.  A node is named
by a text of 1 to 128 bytes of letters, digits, dot, colon, hyphen and
underscore, so that a route can be given as the names one a line.

The edges live beside the rest of the data; nothing here asks whether a
node exists elsewhere.  Built on Standard.Database; its statements are
written for SQLite.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);

module Wolly.Edges is
    """
    A route between two nodes, or none.
    """
    union EdgeRoute: Linear is
        """
        No route leads there, or a node is unknown.
        """
        case NoRoute;
        """
        weight is the sum of the weights of its edges, or their number for
        the route of fewest edges; nodes are their names one a line, the
        first and the last included.
        """
        case Found is
            weight: Nat64;
            nodes: String;
    end;

    """
    The most nodes a query of reachability gives: 10000.
    """
    function mostNodes(): Int64
        ensures result = 10000;

    """
    Whether name may name a node: 1 to 128 bytes of a to z, A to Z, 0 to
    9, dot, colon, hyphen and underscore.
    No contract: a walk over name; false is the answer for a bad one.
    """
    generic [N: Region]
    function isNodeName(name: Span[Nat8, N]): Bool;

    """
    Makes the table of edges and its index, if they are not there.  None
    when both exist afterwards.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function prepareEdges(db: &![Database[Writing], R]): Option[DbError];

    """
    The edge from source to target of kind with weight; an edge of the
    same three there before takes the new weight.  Right false when a name
    is no node name, and then nothing is stored.
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region, T: Region, K: Region]
    function addEdge(db: &![Database[Writing], R], source: Span[Nat8, S], target: Span[Nat8, T], kind: Span[Nat8, K],
                     weight: Int64): Either[DbError, Bool]
        requires weight >= 0;

    """
    Removes the edge from source to target of kind.  Right true when there
    was one.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, S: Region, T: Region, K: Region]
    function removeEdge(db: &![Database[Writing], R], source: Span[Nat8, S], target: Span[Nat8, T],
                        kind: Span[Nat8, K]): Either[DbError, Bool];

    """
    The nodes reachable from origin along edges of kind, origin itself only
    when a cycle leads back to it, sorted, one a line, at most mostNodes.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [M: Free, R: Region, S: Region, K: Region]
    function reachable(db: &![Database[M], R], origin: Span[Nat8, S], kind: Span[Nat8, K]): Either[DbError, String];

    """
    The nodes from which node is reachable along edges of kind: in a
    hierarchy whose edges point from a parent to a child, the parents of
    node and theirs.  Sorted, one a line, at most mostNodes.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [M: Free, R: Region, N: Region, K: Region]
    function ancestors(db: &![Database[M], R], node: Span[Nat8, N], kind: Span[Nat8, K]): Either[DbError, String];

    """
    The lightest route from origin to goal along edges of kind, after the
    sum of their weights (Dijkstra, Standard.Graph.lightestPath).
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [M: Free, R: Region, S: Region, G: Region, K: Region]
    function lightestRoute(db: &![Database[M], R], kind: Span[Nat8, K], origin: Span[Nat8, S],
                           goal: Span[Nat8, G]): Either[DbError, EdgeRoute];

    """
    The route of fewest edges from origin to goal along edges of kind
    (breadth first, Standard.Graph.shortestPath); its weight is their
    number.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [M: Free, R: Region, S: Region, G: Region, K: Region]
    function fewestEdges(db: &![Database[M], R], kind: Span[Nat8, K], origin: Span[Nat8, S],
                         goal: Span[Nat8, G]): Either[DbError, EdgeRoute];

    """
    A cycle among the edges of kind, as the names of its nodes one a line,
    the first again at the end; None when there is none.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [M: Free, R: Region, K: Region]
    function findCycleOf(db: &![Database[M], R], kind: Span[Nat8, K]): Either[DbError, Option[String]];

    """
    Gives back what a route holds.
    No contract: it only gives the value back.
    """
    function destroyRoute(route: EdgeRoute): Unit;
end module.
